# What Docker must NOT receive as build context.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` shipped 812MB — 697MB of local `node_modules`,
# 69MB of `.next`, 19MB of `storybook-static` — on every build. None of it is
# wanted: the image installs its own dependencies in the `deps` stage and runs
# its own `bun run build`, so these are at best dead weight over the wire.
#
# `.next` is worse than dead weight. Copying a locally-built `.next` into the
# build stage lays host artefacts under the build that is about to run, and
# they were produced by a different OS, a different arch and possibly a
# different Next version. That is the kind of mismatch that fails a container
# build while the same commit builds cleanly on the machine it was written on.
#
# `.env` is excluded on purpose too: build-time secrets belong in the builder's
# environment, never baked into an image layer.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in the `deps` stage from package.json + bun.lock.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — the image builds its own.
.next
out
storybook-static
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local environment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local databases and dumps that occasionally land at the root.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.dat

# Test and tooling output nothing in the image reads.
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# The native client is built and shipped separately.
android
twa

# Documentation — it never reaches the runtime image.
*.md
!README.md
